WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.953
CrossCart is a shopping agent built for HacKU agentic commerce.

2
00:00:03.953 --> 00:00:10.278
It compares offers, asks you to approve one exact deal, and keeps payment and recovery traceable.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.039
The buyer asks in Cantonese for headphones below eighteen hundred Hong Kong dollars, with official warranty and delivery within two days.

4
00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:23.867
The agent interprets the request, and the buyer confirms it.

5
00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:28.077
Merchant B costs less, but its third-party warranty fails the requirement.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.256
Merchant A meets the confirmed requirements at seventeen forty-nine, including delivery.

7
00:00:37.256 --> 00:00:42.513
The approval records the exact product, seller, payee, amount and terms.

8
00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:45.380
The AI uses read-only shopping tools.

9
00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.769
Server rules control payment authority.

10
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.771
The buyer opens official Stripe test Checkout and enters synthetic test details.

11
00:00:53.771 --> 00:00:56.156
Stripe authorizes the exact approved amount.

12
00:00:56.156 --> 00:01:00.132
CrossCart then rechecks the mandate and merchant quote before capture.

13
00:01:00.132 --> 00:01:04.903
This is the real Stripe sandbox, with no real money or goods.

14
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.483
The result shows captured payment and a confirmed demo order as separate states.

15
00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:19.122
Judge evidence records the mandate, approval, rules and verified webhook receipts.

16
00:01:19.122 --> 00:01:22.918
A browser return message alone never establishes payment success.

17
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.723
Now the approved price changes from seventeen forty-nine to eighteen forty-nine.

18
00:01:29.723 --> 00:01:32.728
CrossCart blocks the purchase before opening Checkout.

19
00:01:32.728 --> 00:01:34.445
Payment remains not executed.

20
00:01:34.445 --> 00:01:41.315
The original approval stays unchanged, and the buyer can inspect the rejected amount and rule decision.

21
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.957
A third verified scenario captures payment, then simulates merchant order failure.

22
00:01:51.957 --> 00:01:53.760
The order stays failed.

23
00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.718
CrossCart retrieves the same-charge refund from Stripe before showing refund confirmed.

24
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.922
The comparison benchmark uses the same three synthetic offers and the same final choice.

25
00:02:05.922 --> 00:02:08.884
The manual layout requires four navigation actions.

26
00:02:08.884 --> 00:02:11.422
The CrossCart table requires one selection.

27
00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:18.190
It records browser time, but this is a comparison-stage walkthrough, with shared approval and Checkout excluded.

28
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.970
The judge guide links dated primary sources for processing fees, card rewards and Clubpoints.

29
00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:31.381
The domestic-card fee estimate belongs to the merchant.

30
00:02:31.381 --> 00:02:37.778
Reward eligibility is unverified, so no rebate or points discount reduces the approved buyer total.

31
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.684
The demo uses Vercel HTTPS, a persistent Neon ledger and separate visitor sessions.

32
00:02:47.684 --> 00:02:52.055
A signed webhook completed an order with no browser return.

33
00:02:52.055 --> 00:02:54.241
Products and orders remain synthetic.

34
00:02:54.241 --> 00:02:57.302
HKT integration is the next proposed step.
